      "text": "Goods & Service Tax, CBIC, Government of India :: Home Attention This Tab “ACES Archives” displays web content as was available in the erstwhile www.aces.gov.in and for information only. For all transactions under Central Excise and Service Tax use the Tab “ACES (CE&ST) Login” OK May I help you? From August 1st 2025 onwards, CBIC Mitra Helpdesk number will be 1800 425 0232 For any queries and quick assistance, Click Here हिन्दी Sitemap Help GST Acts Services + GST Rates Know Your Jurisdiction SVLDRS Sabka Vishwas - (Legacy Dispute Resolution) Scheme, 2019 (SVLDRS) SVLDRS Login ACES (CE&ST) + ACES Archives Advisories for ACES (CE&ST) Tax Payers ACES (CE&ST) Login Archives + GST - Concept & Status, Overview Detailed PPT as on 01.06.2019 Short PPT Frequently Asked Questions FAQs and User Manual on new GST Registration Services Sectoral FAQs Frequently Asked Questions Advertisements FAQs relating to GST Migration/Registration FAQs for Traders FAQs on Composition Levy (Hindi) FAQs Full Page AD (Hindi) Input Tax Credit (English) Input Tax Credit (Hindi) Export (English) Export (Hindi) Restaurant (English) Restaurant (Hindi) Miscellaneous Communication to Taxpayers HSNS + HSNS CESS Legislation HSNS CESS Login SBS Login View All “Important Notice | Central Excise/Service Tax/SBS/SVLDRS/HSNS Taxpayers: Please use the “Forgot Password” link on the login page to reset your old password before logging in.” “Kind Attention : Directorate General of Systems, CBIC has planned a maintenance activity in the ACES-GST Application between 18:00 Hours to 23:00 Hours on 11th July 2026 (coming weekend). Accordingly, services relating to Central Excise/Service Tax/HSNS/SBS/SVLDRS will not be available during the maintenance window. Taxpayers are advised to plan their activities accordingly”. “Kind Attention : Advisory No. 11/2026 dated 24.06.2026 on 2 Factor Authentication for Central Excise, SBS & HSNS Taxpayers is available under ACES(CE&ST)>Advisories for ACES(CE & ST) and HSNS>HSNS CESS Legislation”. Please Click here for Advisory. “Kind attention to the Chewing tobacco, Jarda and Gutkha Manufacturers: Advisory No. 10/2026 dated 09.06.2026 on CE INT 01/CE INT 02 (Filing Procedure for Sealing/De-Sealing request) is available under “ACES(CE&ST)>Advisories for ACES(CE & ST)”. Please Click here for Advisory. KIND ATTENTION : CENTRAL EXCISE TAXPAYERS: New Functionality for e-Filing of Request for Sealing (Intimation CE INT-01) & De-Sealing (Intimation CE INT-02) is enabled from 07.06.2026. Please refer to the Advisory being issued shortly “Kind Attention HSNS Taxpayers : Advisory No. 09/2026 dated 05.06.2026 on HSNS INT 01/INT 02 (Filing Procedure for Sealing/De-Sealing request) for HSNS Cess Registered Persons is available under HSNS>HSNS CESS Legislation”. Please Click here for Advisory. KIND ATTENTION : CENTRAL EXCISE / HSNS CESS/ SERVICE TAX & SBS TAXPAYERS: Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) at the time of User Login is being introduced now. Please Click Here For Details Please Click here for Advisory. KIND ATTENTION : HSNS CESS TAXPAYERS: New Functionality for e-Filing of Request for Sealing (Intimation INT-01) & De-Sealing (Intimation INT-02) is enabled from 29.05.2026. Please refer to the Advisory being issued shortly KIND ATTENTION: CENTRAL EXCISE / HSNS CESS / SERVICE TAX Taxpayers: Due to urgent maintenance activity, ACES-GST application will NOT BE AVAILABLE from 18:00 hrs 22:00 hrs on 25.05.2026. Kindly plan your activities. The inconvenience caused is regretted. KIND ATTENTION: CENTRAL EXCISE / HSNS CESS / SERVICE TAX Taxpayers: Due to a Scheduled maintenance activity e-Payment facility including Internet Banking, NEFT/RTGS, Payment Aggregator services will NOT BE AVAILABLE (I) From 22:00 Hrs 22.05.2026 to 08:00 Hrs 23.05.2026 and (II) From 22:00 Hrs 23.05.2026 to 08:00 Hrs 24.05.2026. Inconvenience caused is regretted. Kind attention to the Chewing tobacco, Jarda and Gutkha Manufacturers: Advisory No. 08/2026 dated 24.04.2026 on CE Amendment Declaration filing Procedure is available under “ACES(CE&ST)>Advisories for ACES(CE & ST) Please Click here for Advisory. Kind Attention HSNS Taxpayers: Advisory No. 07/2026 dated 17.04.2026 on HSNS Amendment Declaration filing Procedure for HSNS Cess Registered Persons is available under HSNS>HSNS CESS Legislation. Please Click here for Advisory. \"KIND ATTENTION: CENTRAL EXCISE TAXPAYERS : 31st MARCH 2026 IS THE DUE DATE FOR PAYMENT OF CENTRAL EXCISE DUTY FOR THE MONTH OF MARCH 2026. please click here Click here for Advisory. Kind Attention HSNS Taxpayers : Advisory No. 06/2026 dated 12.03.2026 on HSNS Return filing Procedure for HSNS Cess Registered Persons is available under HSNS>HSNS CESS Legislation. please click here Click here for Advisory. Kind attention to the Chewing tobacco, Jarda and Gutkha Manufacturers: As per the Notification No. 05/2025-Central Excise (N.T.) dated 31.12.2025, As per sub-section (2) of Rule 13, the manufacturer shall submit a statement in FORM CE PMT-01 on the existing cbic-gst.gov.in portal by 10th of the same month. FORM CE PMT-01 is available under Taxpayer Dashboard >Menu>CE RETURNS>File PMT-01. please click here Click here for Advisory. Kind Attention HSNS Taxpayers : Advisory No. 04/2026 dated 09.02.2026 on HSNS Declaration filing Procedure for HSNS Cess Registered person is available under HSNS>HSNS CESS Legislation”. Click here for Advisory. Kind attention to the Chewing tobacco, Jarda and Gutkha Manufacturers: Advisory No. 03/2026 dated 05.02.2026 on Central Excise Declaration filing Procedure for Central Excise Taxpayers is available under ACES(CE&ST)>Advisories for ACES(CE & ST) Taxpayers. , Please click here Click here for Advisory. Kind Attention: Central Excise Tobacco (Chewing Tobacco/ Jarda/ Gutkha) Sector Taxpayers covered under New Packaging Capacity based Levy w.e.f. 1st February 2026. This Central Excise duty under Section 3A, is also to be paid like regular Basic Excise Duty (BED) under the Accounting Head \"00380003\" only. Kind attention to the Chewing tobacco, Jarda and Gutkha Manufacturers: As per the Notification No. 05/2025-Central Excise (N.T.) dated 31.12.2025, every manufacturer of the notified goods shall file a declaration in FORM CE DEC-01 on the portal on or before the 7th day of February, 2026. Declaration Form in CE DEC-01 is available under Taxpayer Dashboard >Menu>Registration>File Declaration Due Date for Payment of HSNS CESS for the month of February 2026 is 7th February 2026 Kind Attention: HSNS CESS Application is functional from 01/02/2026 onwards. Taxpayers covered under HSNS CESS levy may login & register on this portal and can use the Temporary Registration Number so generated to make payment of HSNS CESS thereafter. Kind Attention: Advisory 01/2026 - HSNS Cess - Login procedure and Filing Application for New Registration and Payment in the CBIC Taxpayer’s portal – Reg, Please click here Click here for Advisory. Kind Attention: Advisory 02/2026 - Accounting Head for Payment of HSNS Cess – Reg, Please clcik here Click here for Advisory. Kind Attention of Central Excise Tax Payers: CBICMITRA HELPDESK Toll Free Number is changed from '1800-120-0232' to the New Toll Free Number \"1800-425-0232\" w.e.f. 1st August 2025 Click here for Advisory. Latest Update - 6th February 2024 - alternate steps to locate e-Payment Challan under ICEGATE portal. Report Tax Fraud, click here What's New Reviewing authority, Revisional Authority and Appellate Authority in respect of orders passed by Common Adjudicating Authority (CAA) for show cause notices issued by DGGI -reg. Generation and quoting of Document Identification Number(DIN) on any communication issued by the officers of the Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs (CBIC) to tax payers and other concerned persons - reg.s Instructions for processing of applications for GST registration - regarding. Seeks to notify Central Goods and Services Tax (Second Amendment) Rules 2025 Clarification on applicability of late fee for delay in furnishing of FORM GSTR-9C- reg. Procedure to be followed in department appeal filed against interest and/or penalty only, related to Section 128A of the CGST Act, 2017 -regarding. Clarification regarding GST rates & classification (goods) based on the recommendations of the GST Council in its 55th meeting held on 21st December, 2024, at Jaisalmer -reg. Clarifications regarding applicability of GST on certain services – reg. Regularizing payment of GST on co-insurance premium apportioned by the lead insurer to the co-insurer and on ceding /re-insurance commission deducted from the reinsurance premium paid by the insurer to the reinsurer – reg. Seeks to appoint common adjudicating authority for Show cause notices issued by officers of DGGI. English | Hindi Seeks to extend the due date for furnishing FORM GSTR-3B for the month of October, 2024 for registered persons whose principal place of business is in the district of Murshidabad in the state of West Bengal. English | Hindi Amendment to Circular No. 31/05/2018-GST, dated 9th February, 2018 on 'Proper officer under sections 73 and 74 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act, 2017 and under the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act, 2017'–reg. Image Gallery CBIC MITRA HELPDESK Query Form 1800 425 0232 GSTN HELPDESK Home Sitemap Help Contact Us Related Links Home GST Awareness Sitemap Help Contact Us Related Links © 2020. Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs, Government of India, New Delhi, India. Terms & Conditions | Privacy Policy | Disclaimer Follow Us Last Updated: 13 October 2026 Disclaimer: Information is being made available at this site purely as a measure of public facilitation. While every effort has been made to ensure that the information hosted in this website is accurate and up-to-date, Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs does not hold itself liable for any consequences, legal or otherwise, arising out of use or abuse of any such information.",
