e-Return Intermediaries API Specifications ERI List External Agency Central & State Government Department/Approved Undertaking Agency RBI Approved Banks Tax Deductor & Collector Registration Service Available Downloads Help Do not have an account? Register Already have an account? Login test Search Home Home 1. Form 3 of Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers-Disclosure scheme will be enabled shortly 2. Due dates for filing of Income Tax Returns and Audit Reports for AY 2026-27 are extended in the cases of persons mentioned at Sl.No.2 in the Table below Explanation2 to Sub-section (1) of Section 139 of Income Tax Act 1961 vide Circular No.07/2026 dated 28th September,2026. 3. Form 1 under the “Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme” is now available for filing. 4. ITR-1, ITR-2, ITR-3, ITR-4, ITR-5, ITR-6 and ITR-7 for AY 2026-27 are available for filing through both online and offline utilities. 5. Filing of TDS/TCS Correction Statements pertaining to Tax Year 2026-27 has been enabled. 6. Demand Management Facilitation Centre (DFC), has been set up to guide Taxpayers on issues/grievances regarding their outstanding demands. DFC may be contacted through the e-mail id: taxdemand@cpc.incometax.gov.in or on the toll-free number - 1800 309 0131 or chargeable no. 0821-6671200. 7. Excel utilities for filing Updated return for ITR-1 to 7 for AY 2022-23 as per Finance Act, 2026 are available for filing ! ❚❚ Previous Next What's New Stay updated with the latest announcements Rollout of Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme (FADS), 2026 on the Income Tax Portal The Income Tax Department has enabled the Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme, 2026 (FADS 2026) on the e-Filing Portal. Introduced as a one-time compliance opportunity by the Government, this scheme allows eligible taxpayers to voluntarily disclose specified foreign assets and foreign income that were not reported. Under the scheme, eligible taxpayers can furnish the prescribed declaration form online through the e-Filing Portal. Navigation Path: e-File → Income Tax Forms → File Income Tax Forms → Under Other Acts → Foreign Assets of Small Taxpayers Disclosure Scheme, 2026 (Form 1 of FADS 2026) For detailed information and filing guidance, please refer to the FADS 2026 Documentation and User Guide available on the Income Tax Portal. Take this opportunity to regularize previously undisclosed foreign assets and income through the Government's one-time voluntary disclosure scheme. New Integrated Payment Module Goes Live on e‑Filing Portal Seamless payments now enabled across both the Income‑tax Act, 1961 and the Income‑tax Act, 2025. With this enhancement, taxpayers can conveniently make payments under the existing Income‑tax Act, 1961 for dues up to FY 2025‑26, as well as under the Income‑tax Act, 2025 for Tax Year 2026‑27 onwards—all from a single interface. Quick Links Access all services at your fingertips NUDGE Campaign e-Pay Tax e-Verify Return Instant E-PAN Tax Calendar Income Tax Calculator Know Tax Payment Status Link Aadhaar/View Status Comply to Notice Authenticate notice/order issued by ITD Verify PAN Status Verify Service Request Know Your JAO Know TAN Details Download CSI File Report Account Misuse Submit Information on Tax Evasion or Benami Property Tax Information & Services Latest Updates Stay ahead with real-time notifications and critical announcements 12 Oct 2026 News Circular CBDT Notification No. 133/2026 amends the 1988 notification to specify that Joint Commissioners (Appeals) and Additional Commissioners (Appeals) shall be subordinate to the jurisdictional Principal Chief Commissioner or Chief Commissioner of Income-tax. Click here Read more 12 Oct 2026 News Circular CBDT has issued Notification No. 134/2026 dated 8 October 2026, notifying the Income-tax (Sixth Amendment) Rules, 2026, which introduce a revised Form 161 for filing applications for waiver of penalty under section 440(2) of the Income-tax Act, 2025. Click here Read more 22 Sep 2026 SMS Campaign Dear AAXXXXXX1D, Tax Audit Report in Form 3CA-3CD/3CB-… Read more 22 Sep 2026 SMS Campaign Dear ARCAXXXX12, Audit Reports in Forms 3CA-3CD/3CB-3CD/… Read more 22 Sep 2026 E-Mail Campaign Audit Report Due Soon. File Form 10B/10BB by 30 September 2026 Read more 22 Sep 2026 E-Mail Campaign Time to File Your Tax Audit Report | Due by 30 September 2026 Read more View All Updates Important Deadlines Stay on top of your tax obligations Select a date to view details View Full Tax Calendar Year 2026 October Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun View Full Tax Calendar Things to Know Helpful resources and guides How to ...Videos How to file Rectification Request for Tax credit mismatch correction How to file Rectification Request for Reprocessing the Return How to file ITR in offline mode Revamped e-Filing Portal, Designed with taxpayers in mind View All Our Success Enablers Hear what our users have to say Taxpayer Voices Statistics ” Refunds are being sent in a very timely manner. All 4 family members have received their refunds within 6 weeks. Thank you very much. @FinMinIndia @IncomeTaxIndia https://t.co/QZMzpVX1wA 07 Oct 2026 ” I am so amazed at the efficiency and speed with which the @IncomeTaxIndia department works. My refunded failed owing to closure of the bank account. I got my refund within one hour of Refund Re-issue request. Thank you so much. 🙏 This is @narendramodi 's India. @nsitharaman 06 Oct 2026 ” IT Returns processed - that was very quick. #IncomeTax https://t.co/T6sl3H9cPq 03 Oct 2026 ” IT Returns processed - that was very quick #IncomeTax 02 Oct 2026 ” Quite fast this year was not expecting it so early Already credited kudos to @IncomeTaxIndia https://t.co/zeNsu3f4qF 02 Oct 2026 Previous Next Search description The new and intuitive official website of Income Tax Department which deals with e-Filing of returns/forms and other related functionalities. Follow us on Footer About Us About the Portal History of Direct Taxation Vision